From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:17:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] board: mediatek: mt8195: add generic board dir with default
 environment

MT8195/MT8395 (Genio 1200) boards have no default environment at all
in mainline: there are no kernel_addr_r/fdt_addr_r/ramdisk_addr_r etc.,
so bootstd (extlinux, boot scripts, EFI) cannot load anything.

Add a generic board/mediatek/mt8195 directory, selected through
CONFIG_SYS_BOARD, with a text environment holding load addresses that
avoid the reserved-memory carveouts of the Genio 1200 devicetrees and
leave room for large kernels and initrds, plus a boot_targets order of
SD -> UFS -> eMMC -> USB -> network.

Since boards share this environment, set fdtfile at runtime from
CONFIG_DEFAULT_FDT_FILE in board_late_init(), when a board's defconfig
provides one and the environment doesn't already have it.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
---
 arch/arm/mach-mediatek/Kconfig   |  1 +
 board/mediatek/MAINTAINERS       |  1 +
 board/mediatek/mt8195/Makefile   |  3 +++
 board/mediatek/mt8195/mt8195.c   | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 board/mediatek/mt8195/mt8195.env | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 configs/mt8195.config            |  1 +
 6 files changed, 49 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 board/mediatek/mt8195/Makefile
 create mode 100644 board/mediatek/mt8195/mt8195.c
 create mode 100644 board/mediatek/mt8195/mt8195.env

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-mediatek/Kconfig b/arch/arm/mach-mediatek/Kconfig
index cd84109854d..8b8d50571bc 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-mediatek/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-mediatek/Kconfig
@@ -195,6 +195,7 @@ config SYS_BOARD
 	default "mt7987" if TARGET_MT7987
 	default "mt7988" if TARGET_MT7988
 	default "mt8183" if TARGET_MT8183
+	default "mt8195" if TARGET_MT8195
 	default "mt8512" if TARGET_MT8512
 	default "mt8516" if TARGET_MT8516
 	default "mt8518" if TARGET_MT8518
diff --git a/board/mediatek/MAINTAINERS b/board/mediatek/MAINTAINERS
index eaf645086f6..ae5c4002336 100644
--- a/board/mediatek/MAINTAINERS
+++ b/board/mediatek/MAINTAINERS
@@ -40,5 +40,6 @@ MT8195/MT8395
 M:	Macpaul Lin <Macpaul.Lin@mediatek.com>
 M:	Julien Stephan <jstephan@baylibre.com>
 S:	Maintained
+F:	board/mediatek/mt8195/
 F:	configs/mt8195.config
 F:	configs/mt8395_genio_1200_evk_defconfig
diff --git a/board/mediatek/mt8195/Makefile b/board/mediatek/mt8195/Makefile
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..8c06a008f79
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/mediatek/mt8195/Makefile
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+
+obj-y	+= mt8195.o
diff --git a/board/mediatek/mt8195/mt8195.c b/board/mediatek/mt8195/mt8195.c
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..7e218da28e9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/mediatek/mt8195/mt8195.c
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/*
+ * Common board code for MT8195/MT8395 (Genio 1200) based boards
+ */
+
+#include <env.h>
+#include <init.h>
+
+int board_late_init(void)
+{
+	/*
+	 * Boards share this generic board directory and default environment,
+	 * so set the devicetree filename the OS should use (eg. for extlinux
+	 * or EFI boot) from the per-board defconfig, unless already set.
+	 */
+	if (CONFIG_DEFAULT_FDT_FILE[0] && !env_get("fdtfile"))
+		env_set("fdtfile", CONFIG_DEFAULT_FDT_FILE);
+
+	return 0;
+}
diff --git a/board/mediatek/mt8195/mt8195.env b/board/mediatek/mt8195/mt8195.env
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..283229d51aa
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/mediatek/mt8195/mt8195.env
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+ */
+/*
+ * Default environment for MT8195/MT8395 (Genio 1200) based boards.
+ *
+ * DRAM starts at 0x40000000; the Genio 1200 devicetrees reserve:
+ *   0x43200000-0x43dfffff, 0x50000000-0x543fffff (SCP/VPU),
+ *   0x54600000-0x547fffff (BL31) and 0x60000000-0x633fffff (ADSP/AFE/APU).
+ * Load addresses are placed in the gaps:
+ *   scriptaddr      0x43000000  2 MiB
+ *   kernel_addr_r   0x44000000  192 MiB
+ *   fdt_addr_r      0x56000000  32 MiB
+ *   fdtoverlay      0x58000000  128 MiB
+ *   ramdisk_addr_r  0x64000000  up to the 4 GiB ram_top limit
+ */
+scriptaddr=0x43000000
+pxefile_addr_r=0x43000000
+kernel_addr_r=0x44000000
+fdt_addr_r=0x56000000
+fdtoverlay_addr_r=0x58000000
+ramdisk_addr_r=0x64000000
+
+/* SD card first, then UFS, eMMC, USB and finally network */
+boot_targets=mmc1 scsi mmc0 usb pxe dhcp
diff --git a/configs/mt8195.config b/configs/mt8195.config
index 885ba2d157c..91d4781de6f 100644
--- a/configs/mt8195.config
+++ b/configs/mt8195.config
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ CONFIG_SYS_LOAD_ADDR=0x60000000
 CONFIG_FIT=y
 CONFIG_BOOTSTD_FULL=y
 # CONFIG_BOARD_INIT is not set
+CONFIG_BOARD_LATE_INIT=y
 CONFIG_CMD_CLK=y
 CONFIG_CMD_GPT=y
 CONFIG_CMD_MMC=y
